# Python-based scanners for the scan-and-gate CI job. Installed into their own venv so their large
# dependency trees can't change requirements-dev.txt. Edit THIS file, then regenerate the lock:
#   uv pip compile requirements-scanners.in --generate-hashes --python-version 3.12 \
#     --python-platform x86_64-manylinux_2_28 --exclude-newer <today minus 14 days> \
#     --exclude-newer-package certifi=2026-10-21 --exclude-newer-package gitpython=2026-10-15 \
#     -o requirements-scanners.txt
# Then re-add the security-exception line at the end of requirements-scanners.txt (uv drops it;
# without it the gate blocks on ecdsa again, which is the safe failure).
# Install with: pip install --require-hashes -r requirements-scanners.txt
# Semgrep is NOT here: it pins its own dependencies tightly and gets a separate venv.
#
# Cooldown exceptions (--exclude-newer-package), each the oldest release that fixes a finding the
# gate blocked on. Drop them once the cooldown date passes them:
#   certifi 2026.10.19   GHSA-6q48-6c7w-9gw2 (CRITICAL), released 2026-10-20
#   gitpython 3.2.1      CVE-2026-114145 (HIGH), released 2026-10-14
bandit
checkov
